%YAML 1.1
%TAG !u! tag:unity3d.com,2011:
--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: b360da9bf94d30246b40adae73f848a5, type: 3}
  m_Name: TutorialDatabase
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::TutorialDatabase
  tutorials:
  - id: T_SHOPPING
    triggerFlag: tutorial.shopping_available
    behaviourId: Shopping
    priority: 80
    activationPhase: Market
    completionFlags:
    - tutorial.shopping_lesson_complete
    steps:
    - stepId: recipes
      text: 'Welcome to your bistro! Before shopping, let''s plan today''s cooking.
        Open your recipe book: Recipes, in the top bar.'
    - stepId: plan
      text: Each card is a dish. Press + on one dish you'd like to cook today. Dishes
        you can't afford yet are greyed out.
    - stepId: close
      text: Your plan is set! The panel in the top-left now tracks what this dish
        still needs. Close the recipe book to go shopping.
    - stepId: shop
      text: Now let's buy what your dish needs. Click a food type in the plan panel
        to see where to find it, or click a store on the map.
    - stepId: store
      text: 'Welcome in! Each aisle is a shelf: click one to see what''s on it. The
        same food can cost different amounts in different stores.'
    - stepId: shelf
      text: Press + on a food card, or drag it onto your cart, to add a package.
        Click a card to flip it and read its label. When the plan panel shows nothing
        missing, check out. After that first purchase, you can shop as often as you
        like.
  - id: T_SORTING
    triggerFlag: tutorial.sorting_available
    behaviourId: TextOnly
    priority: 90
    activationPhase: FoodSorting
    completionFlags:
    - tutorial.sorting_lesson_complete
    steps:
    - stepId: explain
      text: Sort each new food into Green, Yellow or Red. Green foods are the everyday
        foundation and the only foods that build health. Yellow foods are ones customers
        are moving away from. Red foods are the ones to avoid. Flip a card to read
        its ingredients. Each new food you sort correctly gives back {maxDiscount}
        of what you paid for it. Answers are final once you submit.
  - id: T_BISTRO
    triggerFlag: tutorial.bistro_available
    behaviourId: TextOnly
    priority: 88
    activationPhase: Market
    completionFlags:
    - tutorial.bistro_lesson_complete
    steps:
    - stepId: explain
      text: Back at the market! You can visit other stores and check out again; each
        purchase gets its own quick sort. When you're done shopping, click your Bistro
        on the map to start cooking.
  - id: T_COOKING
    triggerFlag: tutorial.cooking_available
    behaviourId: FirstMeal
    priority: 70
    activationPhase: Service
    completionFlags:
    - tutorial.cooking_lesson_complete
    steps:
    - stepId: choose
      text: Time to cook! Pick a recipe you have ingredients for. Faded recipes are
        missing something.
    - stepId: build
      text: Drag one serving at a time from your pantry into the recipe's slots.
        A red outline means a slot still needs something. Drag a row out of a slot
        to put it back. For your first dish, fill every slot exactly, then press
        Review dish.
    - stepId: feedback
      text: 'Your first dish is done! You used {ingredients}. Health changed by {healthDelta},
        and it covered these Daily Dozen groups: {dailyDozen}. Only Green foods build
        health. Each Daily Dozen group a guest hasn''t had before adds a little extra,
        so vary the plants you serve. From now on, you can also serve dishes that
        don''t match the recipe, but guests will notice.'
  - id: T_CRASH
    triggerFlag: tutorial.first_crash_dialogue_completed
    behaviourId: TextOnly
    priority: 100
    activationPhase: Service
    completionFlags:
    - tutorial.rush_crash_lesson_complete
    steps:
    - stepId: explain
      text: That guest felt a quick burst of energy, then a slump. A rush can feel
        good in the moment, but it doesn't mean the meal was good for them. Judge
        a meal by what's in it, not by how lively a guest seems afterwards.
  - id: T_RENT
    triggerFlag: tutorial.rent_upcoming
    behaviourId: TextOnly
    priority: 95
    activationPhase: Market
    completionFlags:
    - tutorial.rent_lesson_complete
    steps:
    - stepId: explain
      text: 'A letter from the landlord: from tomorrow, rent of ${rent} is due every
        morning. You can only shop while you have money, so keep a little cushion.
        Busy evenings bring in takeaway income, and guests will soon start arriving
        with requests.'
  - id: T_SELL
    triggerFlag: tutorial.money_low
    behaviourId: TextOnly
    priority: 96
    activationPhase: Market
    completionFlags:
    - tutorial.sell_lesson_complete
    steps:
    - stepId: explain
      text: Money is running low, and tomorrow's rent could leave you unable to shop.
        Open Pantry, drag food you won't use onto SELL, then press Sell. Food that
        would spoil before you cook it is the best thing to sell.
  - id: T_REQUESTS
    triggerFlag: okinawa_chef_arrived
    behaviourId: TextOnly
    priority: 85
    activationPhase: Service
    completionFlags:
    - tutorial.requests_lesson_complete
    steps:
    - stepId: explain
      text: From today, guests may ask for something, like Savory, Creamy or Crunchy.
        Each recipe shows what it answers. Answering a request delights a guest and
        grows your popularity. Each request a dish leaves unanswered costs {missedCraving}
        popularity, even when the dish itself is built right. Health still comes
        only from the foods you choose.
  - id: T_FARMER
    triggerFlag: tutorial.food_aid_given
    behaviourId: TextOnly
    priority: 99
    activationPhase: Service
    completionFlags:
    - tutorial.farmer_lesson_complete
    steps:
    - stepId: explain
      text: Your pantry couldn't make any recipe, so a local farmer brought a small
        crate of plain staples, enough for one simple dish. The farmer can only help
        once a day, so shop or sell spare food to get back on your feet.
  - id: T_DAY
    triggerFlag: tutorial.toolbar_day
    behaviourId: TextOnly
    priority: 110
    activationPhase: Any
    completionFlags: []
    steps:
    - stepId: explain
      text: 'You have {totalDays} days to make your bistro''s name. Each day: shop,
        sort what''s new, then cook for your guests. Rent starts on day {rentStart},
        and guests bring requests from day {cravingsStart}. At the end, your popularity
        and the community''s wellbeing decide how the story ends.'
  - id: T_POPULARITY
    triggerFlag: tutorial.toolbar_popularity
    behaviourId: TextOnly
    priority: 110
    activationPhase: Any
    completionFlags: []
    steps:
    - stepId: explain
      text: Popularity is how well known your bistro is. More guests come at {guestThresholds}
        popularity (up to {maxGuests}), and above {walkInThreshold}, walk-in customers
        buy takeaway every evening. Delighted guests, answered requests and tasty
        plates raise it; mismatched dishes and ignored requests lower it.
  - id: T_WALLET
    triggerFlag: tutorial.toolbar_wallet
    behaviourId: TextOnly
    priority: 110
    activationPhase: Any
    completionFlags: []
    steps:
    - stepId: explain
      text: Guests pay you, plus tips, for every dish, and the market takes your
        money for food. From day {rentStart}, rent of ${rent} is due each morning.
        You can only shop while you have money, and ending deep in debt closes the
        bistro. Short on cash? Sell spare food from the Pantry.
  - id: T_SEEN_PANTRY
    triggerFlag: tutorial.seen_pantry
    behaviourId: TextOnly
    priority: 50
    activationPhase: Any
    completionFlags:
    - tutorial.seen_pantry_lesson_complete
    steps:
    - stepId: explain
      text: 'This is your pantry: the food you own. Each card shows its servings
        and how many days are left before it spoils. At the market you can sell pantry
        food back for {sellRate} of what you paid.'
  - id: T_SEEN_GUESTS
    triggerFlag: tutorial.seen_guests
    behaviourId: TextOnly
    priority: 50
    activationPhase: Any
    completionFlags:
    - tutorial.seen_guests_lesson_complete
    steps:
    - stepId: explain
      text: These are today's guests. Some ask for something special. Meeting a request
        helps your popularity; ignoring it can hurt it.
  - id: T_LOCKED_STORE
    triggerFlag: tutorial.clicked_locked_store
    behaviourId: TextOnly
    priority: 50
    activationPhase: Market
    completionFlags:
    - tutorial.locked_store_lesson_complete
    steps:
    - stepId: explain
      text: Hmm, that store isn't open yet. I wonder what's inside... Keep an eye
        on the News.
  - id: T_CLOSED_STORE
    triggerFlag: tutorial.clicked_closed_store
    behaviourId: TextOnly
    priority: 50
    activationPhase: Market
    completionFlags:
    - tutorial.closed_store_lesson_complete
    steps:
    - stepId: explain
      text: Closed today? Darn. Events can close a store for a while. Try another
        store, and check the News to see when it reopens.
  - id: T_STORE_CLOSED_EVENT
    triggerFlag: tutorial.store_closed_event
    behaviourId: TextOnly
    priority: 55
    activationPhase: Market
    completionFlags:
    - tutorial.store_closed_event_lesson_complete
    steps:
    - stepId: explain
      text: 'Heads up: an event has closed a store today. Open the News to see what
        happened.'
  - id: T_NEW_RECIPES
    triggerFlag: tutorial.new_recipes
    behaviourId: TextOnly
    priority: 55
    activationPhase: Market
    completionFlags:
    - tutorial.new_recipes_lesson_complete
    steps:
    - stepId: explain
      text: New recipes are in your book today! Open Recipes to see what's new, and
        plan them with +.
  - id: T_SECOND_CHECKOUT
    triggerFlag: tutorial.first_second_checkout
    behaviourId: TextOnly
    priority: 50
    activationPhase: Market
    completionFlags:
    - tutorial.second_checkout_lesson_complete
    steps:
    - stepId: explain
      text: Back for more? You can shop at as many stores as you like each day. Each
        purchase gets its own quick sort.
  - id: T_SORT_MISTAKE
    triggerFlag: tutorial.first_sort_mistake
    behaviourId: TextOnly
    priority: 50
    activationPhase: FoodSorting
    completionFlags:
    - tutorial.sort_mistake_lesson_complete
    steps:
    - stepId: explain
      text: Not every answer was right this time. Foods you got wrong come back on
        a later purchase, so you'll get another try.
  - id: T_SKIP_CUSTOMER
    triggerFlag: tutorial.first_skip_customer
    behaviourId: TextOnly
    priority: 50
    activationPhase: Service
    completionFlags:
    - tutorial.skip_customer_lesson_complete
    steps:
    - stepId: explain
      text: You skipped a guest. That saves your ingredients, but they leave without
        a meal.
  - id: T_INCOMPLETE_DISH
    triggerFlag: tutorial.first_incomplete_dish
    behaviourId: TextOnly
    priority: 50
    activationPhase: Service
    completionFlags:
    - tutorial.incomplete_dish_lesson_complete
    steps:
    - stepId: explain
      text: That dish didn't match its recipe exactly. Fill every slot with the right
        food type to build the full recipe.
  - id: T_CITY_DURING_SERVICE
    triggerFlag: tutorial.first_city_during_service
    behaviourId: TextOnly
    priority: 50
    activationPhase: Market
    completionFlags:
    - tutorial.city_during_service_lesson_complete
    steps:
    - stepId: explain
      text: Your guests will wait while you shop. Click your Bistro on the map to
        go back to them.
  - id: T_EXPIRING
    triggerFlag: tutorial.food_expiring
    behaviourId: TextOnly
    priority: 55
    activationPhase: Market
    completionFlags:
    - tutorial.expiring_lesson_complete
    steps:
    - stepId: explain
      text: Some food in your pantry spoils tomorrow. It's a good day to cook with
        it, or you can sell it while you're at the market. A quick peek at the pantry
        each morning helps you spot what to use first.
  - id: T_POPULARITY_DROP
    triggerFlag: tutorial.first_popularity_drop
    behaviourId: TextOnly
    priority: 50
    activationPhase: Service
    completionFlags:
    - tutorial.popularity_drop_lesson_complete
    steps:
    - stepId: explain
      text: 'Your dish was built right, but popularity went down a little. That''s
        because it didn''t answer what this guest asked for: each missed request
        costs {missedCraving} popularity. Before picking a recipe, check the guest''s
        request; each recipe card shows which requests it answers.'
  - id: T_COMFORT
    triggerFlag: tutorial.first_comfort_request
    behaviourId: TextOnly
    priority: 60
    activationPhase: Service
    completionFlags:
    - tutorial.comfort_lesson_complete
    steps:
    - stepId: explain
      text: 'This guest would like something comforting. Comfort isn''t tied to one
        recipe: any dish whose ingredients have an average appeal of {comfort} or
        more answers it. You can see each food''s appeal in the corner of its card.'
  fingerprint: KGKTPH7E2eyGquyCjv9JDiRQ01YTQ7NSrv3bFU9aaqs=
